nce","geometry":"Updated floor corner & diffuser geometry","description":"The combined updates optimise the flow around the rear floor, allowing it to generate more load and provide increased performance.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_british_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"},{"component":"Rear Corner","reason":"Performance – Flow Conditioning","type":"Performance","geometry":"New forward deflector geometry","description":"In combination with the above, the new deflector targets an improvement in local flow conditioning and improved floor performance.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_british_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Aston Martin","updates":[]},{"team":"Haas","updates":[{"component":"Rear Wing","reason":"Performance - Local Load","type":"Performance","geometry":"New Rear Wing profiles","description":"The rear wing profiles were comprehensively revised, with particular emphasis placed on the optimisation of flap geometry, leading to an","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_british_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"},{"component":"Rear Wing Endplate","reason":"Performance - Flow Conditioning","type":"Performance","geometry":"Rear Wing Endplate with external protrusions","description":"increase in aerodynamic load while preserving a high level of overall efficiency across the operating range. The Rear Wing Endplates were refined through the introduction of localized protrusions aimed at promoting upwash, contributing to the increase of load of this assembly.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_british_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Audi","updates":[]},{"team":"Alpine","updates":[]},{"team":"Cadillac","updates":[]}],"sources":{"pu":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_british_grand_prix_-_pu_elements_used_per_driver_up_to_now.pdf","upgr